import Dregg2.Games.AutomataflRules -- ⚑ THE RULES-FAITHFUL AUTOMATAFL SPEC (07-20): Automatafl.lean was mirrored off logic/src/game.rs and never read against the Creator-Approved ruleset; the audit (docs/reference/AUTOMATAFL-RULES-CONFORMANCE-AUDIT.md) found 9 divergences, 6 outcome-changing, 3 that DESTROY PIECES — the smallest firing with ONE move on a 3x3 board. This is the replacement, authored against README §Game Rules + old_python_prototype/model.py. THE TYPE OF A TURN CHANGES: a turn is N ROUNDS over a RoundState (board + conflict markers + locked moves + re-entrants), not `Board -> List Move -> Board`; conflicted coordinates are MARKED and become illegal as source AND destination for ALL, the involved players re-enter, everyone else is LOCKED, and the round RECURSES. The path check is INCLUSIVE OF THE DESTINATION (model.py::CanMove scans the inclusive rectangle) so a non-moving piece on the destination BLOCKS and the mover is replaced at its origin; 2-cycles STAY PUT; empty cycles cannot capture; the automaton square is banned as a SOURCE only; the column rule is SELECTABLE (Column|Row|Freeze). A vacuum CONFLUENCE — which the old spec awarded by MOVE-LIST ORDER, deleting the loser — is now a CONFLICT (DetectAndConflict), which is what makes resolve_perm provable. TWO KEYSTONES, both UNCONDITIONAL: resolve_conserves (piece conservation as a bijection on occupied squares — the old applyMoves_conserves_pieces had to ASSUME rules clause 3.2 as hlandA/hlandB) and resolve_perm (permutation-invariance — the old FairnessObligation was not merely unproven, it was FALSE). SETUP/WIN added (2P = two corners in the same row; 4P = one each; the win fires on the automaton MOVING INTO a corner, not sitting on one). 81 #guards, one per rules clause, carrying the audit's D1/D2/D3/D4a/D4b/D5/D6 witnesses now behaving per the rules; mutation-canaried 3 ways. Automatafl.lean is NOT deleted — the ~24k-line proof tower still imports it; the migration is the next stage.
