import Dregg2.Circuit.Emit.UMemoryTableEmit -- ⚑⚑⚑ LAW #1 CUTOVER: THE UNIVERSAL MEMORY OP LOG'S AIR, EMITTED. `Ir2Air::UMemory` is DELETED (the enum VARIANT); `Ir2Air::LeanTable` walks `circuit/descriptors/table-airs/dregg-ir2-umemory-v1.json`. 20 gates + 12 bus interactions at width 23, every count DERIVED from the layout and #guard-pinned (5 booleans + 1 real-prefix + 1 `.first` serial anchor + 1 `.transition` serial increment + 2 read-discipline [the `Option` cell is a PAIR, where the flat memory has one felt] + 2 canonical-`none` + 1 gap definition + 4 decomposition + 2 nullifier-forcing + 1 insert-only tooth; 7 gap-limb byte queries + 1 DOMAIN nibble query, 1 `ir2_umem_log` receive, 2 `ir2_umem_check` Blum legs, 1 `ir2_umem_addrs` closure QUERY — this table is the CLIENT of the table BOTH universal boundary forms SERVE). `ir2_degree_budget` UNCHANGED for `umemory` (3). ★ It PROVES four of the deleted arm's comment-only claims — `serial_is_positional` (under `Coherent`), `read_returns_its_claimed_cell` (BOTH components, which is what makes this discipline stronger than the flat memory's), `canonical_none_is_forced` (what makes `(present, value)` a faithful `optOf` rather than a pair that happens to agree) and `a_nullifier_write_cannot_install_none` (the `UniversalMemory.InsertOnlyAt` tooth) — and sharpens the forcing the tooth stands on: `is_null_eq_real_on_domain` shows the inverse-witness gate reads `is_null = is_real` EXACTLY at domain 3, not `is_null = 1`. ⚠ AND IT REFUTES TWO SENTENCES. (1) `prev_serial < serial (Disciplined), exactly the flat memory's gap shape` — the second clause is TRUE and it is the refutation: there is NO magnitude gate on `UM_PREV_SERIAL`, so the gap gate DEFINES the claimed serial in the field, and `wrapped_prev_serial_satisfies_every_gate` exhibits a NULLIFIER-domain freshness read at serial 1 claiming a prior serial of p−5 that satisfies EVERY EMITTED GATE. (2) `a nullifier-domain write installing none is UNSAT` — true of REAL ro