import Dregg2.Circuit.Emit.MapOpsTableEmit -- ⛑⛑⛑ LAW #1 CUTOVER: THE MAP RECONCILIATION TABLE'S AIR, EMITTED. `Ir2Air::MapOps` is DELETED (the enum VARIANT, not just its ~320-line body); `Ir2Air::LeanTable` walks `circuit/descriptors/table-airs/dregg-ir2-map-ops-v1.json`. 91 gates + 120 bus interactions at width 898, every count DERIVED from the layout and #guard-pinned (1 row guard + 1 op membership + 16 PATH1 direction booleans + 3 AAFI selector pins + 1 read discipline + 16 PATH2 direction booleans + 3x9 canonical splits + 2x9 lex comparators + 8 empty-slot pins; 84 chip queries in FIVE folds, 35 byte queries, 1 `ir2_map_log` receive). `ir2_degree_budget` UNCHANGED for `map_ops` (4). ★ It PROVES the AAFI selector pin in BOTH directions (`s_is_the_op4_indicator`: the three low-degree constraints force s = [op = 4], so the insert block can be neither switched OFF on an op=4 row nor switched ON elsewhere) — which is the ENTIRE licence for a COMMITTED degree-1 `is_aafi` standing in for the degree-3 polynomial `op(op-1)(op-3)` that would blow the frozen map-ops budget of 4 — plus `selectors_are_boolean_on_every_admitted_op` (the four rational LogUp multiplicities are 0/1 on every admitted op, so no chip leg ever carries a fractional or negative count), `not_insert_is_minus_one_at_aafi` (the comment's `repaired from -1 to 0 via +s` parenthesis, checked: without the repair every AAFI row would PUBLISH an absorb rather than consume it) and `the_absent_op_is_unsat` (op=2 satisfies NO assignment here, so `absent is a different table` is a verdict of the membership gate rather than a routing convention). ⚠ AND THE REFUTATION IS THE LOAD-BEARING HALF, TWICE. (1) `an_aafi_row_with_no_opening_satisfies_every_gate`: NOT ONE of this table's 84 chip legs is a gate, so a row declaring root = new_root = 0 with an honest pointer bracket and an ALL-ZERO opening — no leaf digest, no sibling, no chain node — satisfies every one of the 91 EMITTED gates at is_real = 1, proved by `decide